# Candidate tables of successive squares

For each of the twenty-one literal representatives these tables record the
candidate actions of its powers 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and 32. The base comparison and
every squaring step are independently checked by Lean in `Checks`. The tables
avoid repeatedly expanding a thirty-two-fold product of four transversals.

Generated by `source/generate.py` from the retained ATLAS `J2G1-p100B0` word
candidates; see `source/README.md` for attribution and multiplication conventions.
No table identity or exhaustive conjugacy claim is assumed here.
